Privacy Policy

Last updated: September 12, 2026

National Dominance ("the App") is developed by twelve52 LLC ("we", "us", or "our"). This Privacy Policy explains how information is collected, used, and disclosed when you use the App on iOS and Android.

Information We Collect
The App can be played in full without creating an account. Game data such as your saves, settings, and progress are stored locally on your device and are not transmitted to us unless you choose to sign in.

Optional account. If you choose to sign in with Apple or Google, we receive the name, email address, and user identifier provided by that sign-in service and store them, together with your online profile, alias, and rankings data, on our backend hosted by Supabase. This is used to sync your profile and to show online rankings. You can request deletion of your account and all associated data at any time by emailing us at the address below; we complete deletion requests within 30 days.

Third-Party Services
The App uses the following third-party services that may collect information:

Google AdMob. We display ads through Google AdMob. Google may collect and use data to serve personalized or non-personalized ads, including device identifiers (such as the advertising ID), IP address, and usage data. You can review Google's privacy policy at policies.google.com/privacy. Where required, the App asks for your consent before serving personalized ads.

Apple Game Center (iOS). If you choose to sign in to Game Center, Apple handles your Game Center profile, leaderboard, and achievement data according to Apple's privacy policy at apple.com/privacy.

Google Play Games Services (Android). If you choose to sign in to Play Games, Google handles your Play Games profile, leaderboard, and achievement data according to Google's privacy policy at policies.google.com/privacy.

App Tracking Transparency (iOS). On iOS 14.5 and later, the App will request your permission before allowing third-party services to track your activity across other apps and websites. You can change this permission at any time in your device's Settings.

In-App Purchases
The App offers optional one-time purchases, including an option to remove ads. Transactions are processed entirely by Apple through the App Store or by Google through Google Play. We do not receive or store any payment information.

Children's Privacy
The App does not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13. The App contains third-party advertising which may collect data as described above.

Data Retention
Local game data remains on your device until you delete the App. Account data is retained until you delete your account, after which it is removed from our backend.

Your Choices
You can opt out of personalized advertising by adjusting your device settings (iOS: Settings > Privacy > Tracking; Android: Settings > Google > Ads) or through the privacy options inside the App where offered. You can also purchase the remove-ads option within the App to eliminate all advertising.

Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this page with an updated revision date.

Contact Us
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at general@twelve52cards.com
